guamp: an uncaught Objective-C exception's name, reason and throw frames to the kernel log (AegirPoster SIGABRT, fin45)

fin45 (live-20261103-195840, kpan-20261104-021110): AegirPoster aborted three times at 89-102 s with the same stack, symbolized on the
iPadOS 17.7.11 cache (slide 0x4f64000): __pthread_kill <- abort <- demangling_terminate_handler <- _objc_terminate <- std::terminate <-
_dispatch_client_callout <- FBSMainRunLoopSerialQueue _targetQueue_performNextIfPossible <- CFRunLoop source0: an uncaught exception
in a FrontBoard main-queue block, not a fault inside libvulkan_freedreno (the "image" of the exit line is only the last image loaded).
ExceptionDiag.h already keeps "SHENGTHROW name | reason | frames" in the heap for sheng's kernel scan, which guamp has not: the same
text now also goes out as "problem exc<k> ..." lines (8 of 38 characters), printed by native-adreno 0009 as
"GuampMetal: client AegirPoster: problem exc0 ...". Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0016 and 0030.

diff --git a/ExceptionDiag.h b/ExceptionDiag.h
index 3f35f6e..3736ec8 100644
--- a/ExceptionDiag.h
+++ b/ExceptionDiag.h
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@ namespace exceptiondiag {
 
 static NSUncaughtExceptionHandler *gPrevious;
 static char *gText;   // kept referenced: the text must stay in the heap until the process is gone
+// guamp (UniXNU-guamp patches/adreno-metal/0017): guamp's kernel has no heap scan for SHENGTHROW, so the text also goes to the kernel as
+// "problem exc<k> <38 characters>" lines (native-adreno 0009 prints them as "GuampMetal: client <process>: ..."), set by the plugin.
+// fin45: AegirPoster aborted three times in std::terminate from an uncaught exception in a FrontBoard main-queue block, no reason
+// anywhere in the kernel log.
+static void (*gReport)(const char *line);
 
 static void handler(NSException *exception) {
     @autoreleasepool {
@@ -25,6 +30,15 @@ static void handler(NSException *exception) {
         for (NSUInteger i = 0; i < frames.count && i < 20; ++i) [text appendFormat:@" %llx", (unsigned long long)frames[i].unsignedLongLongValue];
         for (NSUInteger i = 0; i < text.length; ++i) if ([text characterAtIndex:i] < 32 || [text characterAtIndex:i] > 126) [text replaceCharactersInRange:NSMakeRange(i, 1) withString:@"?"];
         if (const char *utf8 = text.UTF8String) gText = strdup(utf8);
+        if (gReport && gText) {
+            const char *body = gText + strlen("SHENGTHROW ");
+            const size_t length = strlen(body);
+            for (unsigned k = 0; k < 8 && (size_t)k * 38 < length; ++k) {
+                char line[48];
+                snprintf(line, sizeof line, "exc%u %.38s", k, body + (size_t)k * 38);
+                gReport(line);
+            }
+        }
     }
     if (gPrevious) gPrevious(exception);
 }
